Subject: [PATCH] Send the metric reporting policy at topology sync

em_config sends the Multi-AP Policy Config only after the channel
preference exchange, as its fifth step. In the RDK lab the RDK agents
never complete that exchange (their em_agent drops the Channel Preference
Query), so they never got a policy through onboarding; and a known agent
onboarding again (its em_agent or OneWifi restarted) finds its radios
configured already, so the steps are skipped. The agent then reports no
associated STA link metrics (RCPI 0) until a posted policy changes, the
only other time the controller sends one.

Every onboarding reaches topology sync. When em_config moves on to the AP
capability query, send the agent its Metric Reporting Policy (with the
vendor TLV a posted metrics change carries), once per agent and
onboarding (each of its radios runs em_config); nothing waits for the ACK
(the controller drops an ACK no radio waits for). Only that policy: the
full one this early (traffic separation, 802.1Q, backhaul BSS settings)
made the gateway's co-located agent reconfigure a radio in the middle of
its WSC exchange, and the radio stayed unconfigured. The policy step
later in em_config is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending

